---
title: Migrating to TanStack Table V9 (Angular)
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-s-new-in-tanstack-table-v9","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What's New in TanStack Table V9"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Table V9 delivers major performance improvements, hundreds of bug fixes, new and refreshed features, and optional helpers for composing and managing tables. Despite the scale of the release, the headless model, core table logic, column definitions, and rendering patterns remain familiar. Here are the key changes:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-better-performance","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Better Performance"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lower memory usage"}]},{"type":"text","value":": The core architecture now shares more behavior across table objects, with some large-table scenarios seeing up to 90% memory savings."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Faster client-side row models"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Sorting, filtering, and aggregation paths have improved algorithms and memoization, with many scenarios seeing up to 40-70% speed improvements."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Better column resizing performance"}]},{"type":"text","value":": The same architectural and memoization work also speeds up column resizing."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-state-management-overhaul","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. State Management Overhaul"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Store foundation"}]},{"type":"text","value":": The internal state system has been rebuilt on "},{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/store","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Store"}]},{"type":"text","value":", providing a reactive, framework-agnostic foundation."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular signal integration"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Table atoms are backed by signals. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computed(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" when you want selector-style derivation or custom equality, and keep reads scoped to the state you actually need."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"External state remains supported"}]},{"type":"text","value":": You can still use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":" plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"on[State]Change"},{"type":"text","value":" by owning slices with Angular signals."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"3-type-safety-improvements","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Type-Safety Improvements"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New and revamped type helpers"}]},{"type":"text","value":": There are helpers for defining columns, custom filters, sorts, aggregations, column and table meta, shared table options and components, and more."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-table meta types"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableMeta"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnMeta"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" slots let you type meta for a specific table instead of globally augmenting shared interfaces. "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No more global declaration merging required!"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Feature-gated APIs"}]},{"type":"text","value":": APIs only exist when their feature is registered, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures()"},{"type":"text","value":" validates feature prerequisites at the type level."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"4-tree-shaking-and-extensibility","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Tree Shaking and Extensibility"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import only the features you use"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Tables that only need sorting do not ship filtering, pagination, or other unused feature code."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tree-shakeable row models and functions"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Row model factories and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFns"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFns"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":" now live on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures()"},{"type":"text","value":", so unused processing code can be dropped."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom features use the same system"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Your own feature plugins can register state, options, and APIs alongside the built-in features. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./custom-features.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Features Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"5-composability","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5. Composability"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Compose reusable table configuration, including features, row models, and default options."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Create reusable, strongly typed Angular table factories with pre-bound features, row models, default options, and component registries."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"6-new-and-refreshed-features","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6. New and Refreshed Features"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New Features"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell Selection"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cellSelectionFeature"},{"type":"text","value":" adds spreadsheet-style rectangular cell range selection, with drag, Shift-extend, and multiple disjoint ranges. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./cell-selection.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell Selection Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell Spanning"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cellSpanningFeature"},{"type":"text","value":" merges body cells across rows and columns ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"spanRows"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"spanColumns"},{"type":"text","value":", with span-aware cell selection), and header groups now compute "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header.rowSpan"},{"type":"text","value":" so shallow columns can span header rows. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./cell-spanning.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell Spanning Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Refreshed Features"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"More capable features"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Aggregation, Row Selection, Column Pinning, and Column Resizing have all been made more feature rich (multiple aggregation definitions per column, Shift range selection, logical "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end"},{"type":"text","value":" pinning, and more)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New core APIs"}]},{"type":"text","value":": New table and row APIs (like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getMaxSubRowDepth()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getDisplayIndex()"},{"type":"text","value":") round out the core feature set."}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"7-modern-builds","children":[{"type":"text","value":"7. Modern Builds"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ESM-only"}]},{"type":"text","value":": UMD and CJS builds have been dropped. Packages ship as modern ESM."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript target "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ES2022"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Compiled output now targets ES2022."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Smaller install size"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Published packages no longer ship "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src"},{"type":"text","value":" or source maps, which reduces install footprint."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"the-good-news-most-upgrades-are-opt-in","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Good News: Most Upgrades Are Opt-in"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"While v9 is a significant upgrade, "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"you don't have to adopt everything at once"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Don't want to think about tree-shaking yet?"}]},{"type":"text","value":" You can start with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stockFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" to include most commonly used features."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your table markup is largely unchanged."}]},{"type":"text","value":" How you render "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<table>"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<thead>"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<tr>"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<td>"},{"type":"text","value":", etc. remains the same."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The main change is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"how you define a table"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with the Angular adapter, specifically the new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" option and how row model factories are registered inside it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"core-breaking-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core Breaking Changes"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"entrypoint-change","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Entrypoint Change"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Angular adapter entrypoint to create a table instance is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectTable"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v8\nimport { createAngularTable } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst v8Table = createAngularTable(() => ({\n  // options\n}))\n\n// v9\nimport { injectTable } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst v9Table = injectTable(() => ({\n  // options\n}))","lang":"ts"},{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectTable"},{"type":"text","value":" evaluates your initializer whenever any Angular signal read inside of it changes.\nKeep expensive/static values (like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columns"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":") as stable references outside the initializer."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"new-required-features-table-option","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New Required "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" Table Option"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In Table V9, you must explicitly declare which features your table uses. Features, Row Models, and Row Model processing \"Fns\" are defined on the new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" table option."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In Table V8, all features were bundled and included in the table setup. In Table V9, you import only what you need."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Table V8\nimport {\n  createAngularTable,\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  sortingFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst v8Table = createAngularTable(() => ({\n  columns,\n  data: data(),\n  getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n  getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(),\n  sortingFns,\n}))\n\n// Table V9\nimport {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  injectTable,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\n// All table options that concern including code modules (features, row models, Fns, etc.)\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature, // new - import and pass the feature you want to use\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(), // now row models are defined on the features object\n  sortFns, // now Fns are defined on the features object\n  // ...more features, row models, etc.\n})\n\n// Define stable references outside the initializer\nconst v9Table = injectTable(() => ({\n  features, // new required option\n  columns: this.columns,\n  data: this.data(),\n}))","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"shortcut-use-stockfeatures-for-table-v8-like-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shortcut: Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stockFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" for Table V8-like Behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want all features without thinking about it (like Table V8), import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stockFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { injectTable, stockFeatures } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features: stockFeatures, // All features included - just like Table V8\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"available-features","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available Features"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Feature"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import Name"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Faceting"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnFacetingFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Filtering"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnFilteringFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Grouping"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnGroupingFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Ordering"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnOrderingFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Pinning"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnPinningFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Resizing"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnResizingFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Sizing"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnSizingFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Visibility"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnVisibilityFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Global Filtering"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"globalFilteringFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Aggregation"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowAggregationFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Expanding"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowExpandingFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Pagination"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowPaginationFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Pinning"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowPinningFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Selection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowSelectionFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Sorting"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowSortingFeature"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"row-model-factories","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Model Factories"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row models are the functions that process your data (filtering, sorting, pagination, etc.). In Table V9, row model factories and their "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*Fns"},{"type":"text","value":" registries move from a separate "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowModels"},{"type":"text","value":" option into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":". Row model slots are type-checked, so each row model must be specified after its associated feature in the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"migration-mapping","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migration Mapping"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table V8 Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table V9 "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" Slot"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table V9 Factory Function"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCoreRowModel()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(automatic)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not needed, always included"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFilteredRowModel()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filteredRowModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFilteredRowModel()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getSortedRowModel()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortedRowModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSortedRowModel()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPaginationRowModel()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"paginatedRowModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createPaginatedRowModel()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getExpandedRowModel()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expandedRowModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createExpandedRowModel()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getGroupedRowModel()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"groupedRowModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGroupedRowModel()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFacetedRowModel()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"facetedRowModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFacetedRowModel()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFacetedMinMaxValues()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"facetedMinMaxValues"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFacetedMinMaxValues()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFacetedUniqueValues()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"facetedUniqueValues"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFacetedUniqueValues()"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFns"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFns"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":" objects are now registered as named slots on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" rather than passed as arguments to the factory functions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"key-change-row-model-factories-and-fn-registries-move-into-tablefeatures","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key Change: Row Model Factories and Fn Registries Move into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  tableFeatures,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createGroupedRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  filterFns, // Built-in filter functions\n  sortFns, // Built-in sort functions\n  aggregationFns, // Built-in aggregation functions\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  columnGroupingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  groupedRowModel: createGroupedRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n  aggregationFns,\n})\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"full-migration-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full Migration Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v8\nimport {\n  createAngularTable,\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getFilteredRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  getPaginationRowModel,\n  filterFns,\n  sortingFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst v8Table = createAngularTable(() => ({\n  columns,\n  data: data(),\n  getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(), // used to be called \"get*RowModel()\"\n  getFilteredRowModel: getFilteredRowModel(),\n  getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(),\n  getPaginationRowModel: getPaginationRowModel(),\n  filterFns, // used to be passed in as a root option\n  sortingFns,\n}))\n\n// v9\nimport {\n  injectTable,\n  tableFeatures,\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst v9Table = injectTable(() => ({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data: data(),\n}))","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"prefer-individual-fn-imports-over-full-registries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefer Individual Fn Imports Over Full Registries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFns"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFns"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":" registry exports are now deprecated in favor of importing individual "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFn_*"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFn_*"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFn_*"},{"type":"text","value":" functions and registering only the ones you use (or passing functions directly in column definitions with no registration at all). The full registries still work, but spreading them puts every built-in function in your bundle. String names, including the default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'auto'"},{"type":"text","value":", only resolve functions you have registered."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Before: registers every built-in function\nimport { filterFns, sortFns } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  // ...other features and row models\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n})\n\n// After: registers only the functions you use\nimport {\n  filterFn_includesString,\n  sortFn_alphanumeric,\n  sortFn_text,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  // ...other features and row models\n  filterFns: { includesString: filterFn_includesString },\n  sortFns: { alphanumeric: sortFn_alphanumeric, text: sortFn_text },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"instance-methods-must-be-called-on-their-instance","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Instance Methods Must Be Called on Their Instance"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In v9, methods on rows, cells, columns, headers, and similar table objects are shared on the object's prototype instead of being created as arrow functions on each object. This improves memory usage, but it means destructuring those methods loses the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"this"},{"type":"text","value":" context they need to operate on the instance."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v8 - worked because getValue closed over the row object\nconst { getValue } = row\nconst value = getValue('name')\n\n// v9 - call the method on the instance\nconst value = row.getValue('name')","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This applies to row, cell, column, header, and related instance APIs, but not to the table instance itself. Audit code that destructures methods from table objects or passes them around as bare callbacks. Prefer calling them through the original object, for example "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getValue('name')"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell.getContext()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getCanSort()"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header.getContext()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Because these methods now live on the prototype, they also do not appear as own properties in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Object.keys(instance)"},{"type":"text","value":", object spread, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JSON.stringify"},{"type":"text","value":". A shallow clone like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ ...row }"},{"type":"text","value":" copies row data but does not copy row methods. The methods are still callable normally because JavaScript looks them up through the prototype chain."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-management-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management Changes"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"accessing-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accessing State"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In v8, you accessed state via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getState()"},{"type":"text","value":". In v9, read the specific\nstate slice from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.atoms.<slice>.get()"},{"type":"text","value":" where possible. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.store.get()"},{"type":"text","value":"\nwhen you need the full flat state shape, such as debug JSON."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v8\nconst state = table.getState()\nconst v8 = table.getState()\nconst { sorting, pagination } = v8\n\n// v9 - per-slice reads, preferred for Angular render code\nconst sorting = table.atoms.sorting.get()\nconst pagination = table.atoms.pagination.get()\n\n// v9 - full-state flat snapshot\nconst fullState = table.store.get()\nconst v9 = table.store.get()\nconst { sorting: v9Sorting, pagination: v9Pagination } = v9","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"optimizing-reads-with-angular-signals","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optimizing Reads with Angular Signals"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In Angular, you have a few good options for consuming table state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"option-1-read-table-atoms-directly","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option 1: Read table atoms directly"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Angular adapter backs table atoms with Angular signals. Read the atom you care about directly in templates, effects, or computed values."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { computed, effect } from '@angular/core'\nimport { shallow } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n\n  // Use computed when deriving from a slice or applying equality.\n  private readonly pagination = computed(\n    () => this.table.atoms.pagination.get(),\n    {\n      equal: shallow,\n    },\n  )\n\n  constructor() {\n    effect(() => {\n      const { pageIndex, pageSize } = this.pagination()\n      console.log('Page', pageIndex, 'Size', pageSize)\n    })\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"option-2-use-computed-for-selected-object-slices","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option 2: Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computed(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" for selected object slices"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use Angular "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computed(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" when you want selector-style behavior, a derived value, or an equality function. For object/array slices, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shallow"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/angular-table"},{"type":"text","value":" to avoid unnecessary downstream work when the slice is recreated with the same values."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { computed, effect } from '@angular/core'\nimport { shallow } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n\n  // Provide an equality function for object slices\n  readonly pagination = computed(() => this.table.atoms.pagination.get(), {\n    equal: shallow,\n  })\n\n  constructor() {\n    effect(() => {\n      // This effect only re-runs when pagination changes\n      const { pageIndex, pageSize } = this.pagination()\n      console.log('Page', pageIndex, 'Size', pageSize)\n    })\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"controlled-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Controlled State"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The v8-style "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"on[State]Change"},{"type":"text","value":" controlled state patterns still work and remain convenient for simple integrations. For new v9 code, prefer owning state slices with external atoms via the new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"atoms"},{"type":"text","value":" table option (created with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAtom"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/angular-store"},{"type":"text","value":"), which give you fine-grained subscriptions without mirroring state through Angular signals. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./table-state#external-atoms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"External Atoms section of the Table State Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and the "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/basic-external-atoms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic External Atoms example"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { signal } from '@angular/core'\nimport type { SortingState, PaginationState } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly sorting = signal<SortingState>([])\n  readonly pagination = signal<PaginationState>({ pageIndex: 0, pageSize: 10 })\n\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n    state: {\n      sorting: this.sorting(),\n      pagination: this.pagination(),\n    },\n    onSortingChange: (updater) => {\n      updater instanceof Function\n        ? this.sorting.update(updater)\n        : this.sorting.set(updater)\n    },\n    onPaginationChange: (updater) => {\n      updater instanceof Function\n        ? this.pagination.update(updater)\n        : this.pagination.set(updater)\n    },\n  }))\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The v8-style "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStateChange"},{"type":"text","value":" callback is no longer part of the v9 table state model. Use per-slice "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"on[State]Change"},{"type":"text","value":" callbacks or subscribe to the table store when you need to listen to all state changes."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const unsubscribe = this.table.store.subscribe((state) => {\n  console.log(state)\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"feature-by-feature-breaking-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Feature-by-Feature Breaking Changes"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sorting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorting"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sorting-related APIs have been renamed for consistency:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v9"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortingFn"},{"type":"text","value":" (column def option)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFn"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getSortingFn()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getSortFn()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getAutoSortingFn()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getAutoSortFn()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SortingFn"},{"type":"text","value":" type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SortFn"},{"type":"text","value":" type"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SortingFns"},{"type":"text","value":" interface"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SortFns"},{"type":"text","value":" interface"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortingFns"},{"type":"text","value":" (built-in functions)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFns"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Update your column definitions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"column-pinning","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Pinning"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"V9 changes column pinning to use logical "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end"},{"type":"text","value":" terminology instead of the physical "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"left"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"right"},{"type":"text","value":" terminology used in V8. In LTR languages/layouts, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":" usually corresponds to left and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end"},{"type":"text","value":" to right; in RTL languages/layouts, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":" usually corresponds to right and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end"},{"type":"text","value":" to left. There are no deprecated aliases."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"V8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"V9"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnPinning.left"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnPinning.start"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnPinning.right"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnPinning.end"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.pin('left')"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.pin('start')"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.pin('right')"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.pin('end')"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIsPinned() === 'left'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIsPinned() === 'start'"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIsPinned() === 'right'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIsPinned() === 'end'"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getLeftVisibleCells()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getStartVisibleCells()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getRightVisibleCells()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getEndVisibleCells()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getLeftHeaderGroups()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getStartHeaderGroups()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getRightHeaderGroups()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getEndHeaderGroups()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getLeftLeafColumns()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getStartLeafColumns()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getRightLeafColumns()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getEndLeafColumns()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getLeftVisibleLeafColumns()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getStartVisibleLeafColumns()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getRightVisibleLeafColumns()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getEndVisibleLeafColumns()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getLeftTotalSize()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getStartTotalSize()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getRightTotalSize()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getEndTotalSize()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getStart('left')"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getStart('start')"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getAfter('right')"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getAfter('end')"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIndex('left')"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIndex('start')"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIndex('right')"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIndex('end')"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This rename is about logical table regions, not automatic DOM direction handling. For sticky column pinning, prefer CSS logical properties like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"insetInlineStart"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"insetInlineEnd"},{"type":"text","value":". The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnResizeDirection"},{"type":"text","value":" table option is unchanged."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enablePinning"},{"type":"text","value":" option has also been split into separate options:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v8\nenablePinning: true\n\n// v9\nenableColumnPinning: true\nenableRowPinning: true","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"column-sizing-vs-column-resizing-split","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Sizing vs. Column Resizing Split"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In v8, column sizing and resizing were combined in a single feature. In v9, they've been split into separate features for better tree-shaking."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v9"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ColumnSizing"},{"type":"text","value":" (combined feature)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnSizingFeature"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnResizingFeature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnSizingInfo"},{"type":"text","value":" state"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnResizing"},{"type":"text","value":" state"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setColumnSizingInfo()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setColumnResizing()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onColumnSizingInfoChange"},{"type":"text","value":" option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onColumnResizingChange"},{"type":"text","value":" option"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you only need column sizing (fixed widths) without interactive resizing, you can import just "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnSizingFeature"},{"type":"text","value":". If you need drag-to-resize functionality, import both."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"grouping-and-aggregation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grouping and Aggregation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Aggregation is now its own feature, independent from column grouping. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stockFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" still includes both, so tables using it need no feature-registration change. If you declare features explicitly, add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowAggregationFeature"},{"type":"text","value":" whenever columns use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getAggregationValue"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell.getIsAggregated"},{"type":"text","value":". Add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnGroupingFeature"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"groupedRowModel"},{"type":"text","value":" only when you also group rows."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const features = tableFeatures({\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  columnGroupingFeature, // only for grouped rows\n  groupedRowModel: createGroupedRowModel(),\n  aggregationFns: { sum: aggregationFn_sum },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom aggregation callables have changed to context-based definitions:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Table V8/earlier V9 betas\nconst total = (columnId, leafRows, childRows) =>\n  leafRows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + row.getValue(columnId), 0)\n\n// Current V9\nconst total = constructAggregationFn({\n  aggregate: ({ rows, getValue }) =>\n    rows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + Number(getValue(row)), 0),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The old per-function choice between "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"childRows"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"leafRows"},{"type":"text","value":" is replaced by a single depth-selected "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context.rows"},{"type":"text","value":", controlled by the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxAggregationDepth"},{"type":"text","value":" column option. The default ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":") preserves V8's direct-child grouped aggregation; use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Infinity"},{"type":"text","value":" to aggregate terminal leaf rows."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getAggregationValue()"},{"type":"text","value":" now takes a single options object instead of positional arguments:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Table V8/earlier V9 betas\ncolumn.getAggregationValue(rows, maxDepth)\n\n// Current V9\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows, maxDepth })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getAggregationFn()"},{"type":"text","value":" is now "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getAggregationFns()"},{"type":"text","value":" because a column can run multiple definitions, and the old callable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AggregationFn"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CreatedAggregationFn"},{"type":"text","value":" types are replaced by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AggregationFnDef"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./grouping","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grouping Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and the "},{"type":"link","href":"./aggregation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Aggregation Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for full documentation of the new capabilities."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"row-selection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Selection"}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"warning","title":"Warning","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Minor breaking change:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getToggleSelectedHandler()"},{"type":"text","value":" now enables inclusive Shift range selection by default when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowSelectionFeature"},{"type":"text","value":" is enabled. Existing checkboxes or rows wired through this handler establish an anchor on an ordinary interaction and select or deselect the current display-order range on a Shift interaction. Direct "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.toggleSelected()"},{"type":"text","value":" calls are unchanged."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableRowRangeSelection: false"},{"type":"text","value":" to preserve the previous non-range handler behavior. The handler must receive an event that exposes Shift directly or through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nativeEvent"},{"type":"text","value":"; see "},{"type":"link","href":"./row-selection.md#shift-range-selection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shift Range Selection"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The \"some rows selected\" checks were simplified to mean \"at least one row is selected\":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v9"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getIsSomeRowsSelected()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when some but not all rows are selected"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when at least one row is selected"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getIsSomePageRowsSelected()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when some but not all page rows are selected"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" when at least one page row is selected"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In v8 these returned "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" once every row was selected; in v9 they stay "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":". If you use them to drive an indeterminate \"select all\" checkbox, gate the indeterminate state on the matching all-selected check so it clears at full selection:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsSomeRowsSelected() && !getIsAllRowsSelected()"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"row-and-internal-api-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row and Internal API Changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some row APIs have changed from private to public:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v9"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row._getAllCellsByColumnId()"},{"type":"text","value":" (private)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getAllCellsByColumnId()"},{"type":"text","value":" (public)"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All other internal APIs prefixed with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_"},{"type":"text","value":" have been removed. If you were using any of these, use their public equivalents."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removed: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table._getPinnedRows()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removed: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table._getFacetedRowModel()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removed: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table._getFacetedMinMaxValues()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removed: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table._getFacetedUniqueValues()"}]}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"column-helper-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Helper Changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createColumnHelper"},{"type":"text","value":" function now requires a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" type parameter in addition to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v8\nimport { createColumnHelper } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst columnHelperV8 = createColumnHelper<Person>()\n\n// v9\nimport {\n  createColumnHelper,\n  tableFeatures,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ rowSortingFeature })\nconst columnHelperV9 = createColumnHelper<typeof features, Person>()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"new-columns-helper-method","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columns()"},{"type":"text","value":" Helper Method"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"v9 adds a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columns()"},{"type":"text","value":" helper for better type inference when wrapping column arrays."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const columnHelper = createColumnHelper<typeof features, Person>()\n\n// Wrap your columns array for better type inference\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    header: 'First Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('lastName', {\n    id: 'lastName',\n    header: () => 'Last Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.display({\n    id: 'actions',\n    header: 'Actions',\n    cell: () => 'Edit',\n  }),\n])","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"using-with-createtablehook","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":", you get a pre-bound "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppColumnHelper"},{"type":"text","value":" that only requires "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createTableHook,\n  tableFeatures,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  sortFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst { injectAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({ features })\n\n// TFeatures is already bound, only need TData!\nconst columnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rendering-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering Changes"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"flexrender","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rendering primitives in the Angular adapter are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*flexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" directives."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In v9, you can continue to render header/cell/footer content using the Angular adapter rendering utilities, but there are a few important improvements and helper APIs to be aware of."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"structural-directive-rendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structural directive rendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular rendering is directive-based:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*flexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" renders arbitrary render content (primitives, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TemplateRef"},{"type":"text","value":", component types, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRenderComponent(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" wrappers)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The directive is responsible for mounting embedded views or components via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ViewContainerRef"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"shorthand-directives","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shorthand directives"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you're rendering standard table content, prefer the shorthand helpers:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*flexRenderCell=\"cell; let value\""}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*flexRenderHeader=\"header; let value\""}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*flexRenderFooter=\"footer; let value\""}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These automatically select the correct column definition ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnDef.cell"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":") and the right props ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell.getContext()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header.getContext()"},{"type":"text","value":"), so you don't need to manually provide "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props:"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"di-aware-render-functions-context-injection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DI-aware render functions + context injection"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column definition render functions ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":") run inside an Angular injection context, so they can safely call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inject()"},{"type":"text","value":" and use signals."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a component is rendered through the FlexRender directives, you can also access the full render props object via DI using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectFlexRenderContext()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"component-rendering-helper-flexrendercomponent","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component rendering helper: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRenderComponent"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you need to render an Angular component with explicit configuration (custom "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inputs"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputs"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injector"},{"type":"text","value":", and Angular v20+ creation-time "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bindings"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"directives"},{"type":"text","value":"), return a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRenderComponent(Component, options)"},{"type":"text","value":" wrapper from your column definition."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For complete rendering details (including component rendering, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TemplateRef"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRenderComponent"},{"type":"text","value":", and context helpers), see the "},{"type":"link","href":"./flex-render","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FlexRender Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-tableoptions-utility","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions()"},{"type":"text","value":" Utility"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions()"},{"type":"text","value":" helper provides type-safe composition of table options. It's useful for creating reusable partial configurations that can be spread into your table setup."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  injectTable,\n  tableOptions,\n  tableFeatures,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\nimport { isDevMode } from '@angular/core'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ rowSortingFeature })\n\n// Create a reusable options object with features pre-configured\nconst baseOptions = tableOptions({\n  features,\n  debugTable: isDevMode(),\n})\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    ...baseOptions,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"composing-partial-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Composing Partial Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions()"},{"type":"text","value":" lets you omit required fields (like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columns"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":") when creating partial configurations:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  tableOptions,\n  tableFeatures,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n  filterFns,\n})\n\n// Partial options without data or columns\nconst featureOptions = tableOptions({ features })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"import { injectTable, tableOptions } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\n// Another partial (inherits features from spread)\nconst paginationDefaults = tableOptions({\n  initialState: {\n    pagination: { pageIndex: 0, pageSize: 25 },\n  },\n})\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    ...featureOptions,\n    ...paginationDefaults,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"using-with-createtablehook-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions()"},{"type":"text","value":" pairs well with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" for building composable table factories:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createTableHook,\n  tableOptions,\n  tableFeatures,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  sortFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst sharedOptions = tableOptions({ features })\n\nconst { injectAppTable } = createTableHook(sharedOptions)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createtablehook-composable-table-patterns","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":": Composable Table Patterns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is an advanced, optional feature."}]},{"type":"text","value":" You don't need to use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectTable"},{"type":"text","value":" is sufficient for most use cases."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For applications with multiple tables sharing the same configuration, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" lets you define features, row models, and reusable components once."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For full setup and patterns, see the "},{"type":"link","href":"./composable-tables.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Composable Tables Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typescript-changes-summary","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript Changes Summary"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"type-generics","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Generics"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Most types now require a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v8\ntype Column<TData>\ntype ColumnDef<TData>\ntype Table<TData>\ntype Row<TData>\ntype Cell<TData, TValue>\n\n// v9\ntype Column<TFeatures, TData, TValue>\ntype ColumnDef<TFeatures, TData, TValue>\ntype Table<TFeatures, TData>\ntype Row<TFeatures, TData>\ntype Cell<TFeatures, TData, TValue>","lang":"txt"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"using-typeof-features","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"typeof features"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The easiest way to get the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" type is with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"typeof"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n})\n\ntype MyFeatures = typeof features\n\nconst columns: ColumnDef<typeof features, Person>[] = [...]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"using-stockfeatures","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StockFeatures"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stockFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":", use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StockFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" type:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { StockFeatures, ColumnDef } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst columns: ColumnDef<StockFeatures, Person>[] = [...]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tablemeta-columnmeta-typing-changes","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TableMeta"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ColumnMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" Typing Changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No more declaration merging required! (Although it still works if you want to keep using it)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Global declaration merging to extend "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TableMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ColumnMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" works exactly like it did in v8. The only change you need to make is updating the generics shape: both interfaces now take "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" as the first type parameter."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optionally, v9 also adds a new way to declare meta types "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"per-table"}]},{"type":"text","value":" without declaration merging. You can use type-only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableMeta"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" slots on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" option, which only affect tables created with that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" object:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<{ customProperty: string }>(),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the new "},{"type":"link","href":"../../../guide/table-and-column-meta","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table and Column Meta Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for full details on both approaches."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"filterfns-sortfns-aggregationfns-filtermeta-augmentation-replaced-by-registry-slots","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FilterFns"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SortFns"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FilterMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" Augmentation Replaced by Registry Slots"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In v8, making a custom function usable as a string reference (like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFn: 'fuzzy'"},{"type":"text","value":") required "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"declare module"},{"type":"text","value":" augmentation of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FilterFns"},{"type":"text","value":" interface, and typing filter meta required augmenting "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FilterMeta"},{"type":"text","value":". In v9, registering the function in the matching registry slot does both jobs with no global augmentation:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v8\ndeclare module '@tanstack/angular-table' {\n  interface FilterFns {\n    fuzzy: FilterFn<unknown>\n  }\n  interface FilterMeta {\n    itemRank: RankingInfo\n  }\n}\n\n// v9 - register in the slot; the key becomes a valid string value\ninterface FuzzyFilterMeta {\n  itemRank?: RankingInfo\n}\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  filterFns: { fuzzy: fuzzyFilter },\n  filterMeta: metaHelper<FuzzyFilterMeta>(),\n})\n\n// 'fuzzy' now typechecks in column defs for tables using these features\ncolumnHelper.accessor('name', { filterFn: 'fuzzy' })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same pattern applies to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFns"},{"type":"text","value":" (for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFn"},{"type":"text","value":" string values) and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":" (for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFn"},{"type":"text","value":" string values). See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./fuzzy-filtering.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fuzzy Filtering Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for a complete example."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"rowdata-type-restriction","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RowData"},{"type":"text","value":" Type Restriction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RowData"},{"type":"text","value":" type is now more restrictive:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// v8 - very permissive\ntype RowData = unknown\n\n// v9 - must be a record or array\ntype RowData = Record<string, any> | Array<any>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This change improves type safety. If you were passing unusual data types, ensure your data conforms to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, any>"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Array<any>"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"migration-checklist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migration Checklist"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Update your table setup to v9 and define "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures()"},{"type":"text","value":" (or use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stockFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migrate "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get*RowModel()"},{"type":"text","value":" options: move row model factories into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" as named slots"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Move "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterFns"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFns"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":" into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" as named slots (no longer passed as factory arguments)"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace destructured row/cell/column/header methods with calls on the instance (for example, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getValue('name')"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rename "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortingFn"},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sortFn"},{"type":"text","value":" in column definitions"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Update column pinning to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end"},{"type":"text","value":" terminology ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnPinning.start"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.pin('end')"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getStart*"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getEnd*"},{"type":"text","value":" APIs)"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enablePinning"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableColumnPinning"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableRowPinning"},{"type":"text","value":" if used"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rename "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnSizingInfo"},{"type":"text","value":" state → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnResizing"},{"type":"text","value":" (and related options)"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Convert custom aggregation callables to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"constructAggregationFn({ aggregate, merge? })"},{"type":"text","value":" definitions"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Update state access: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getState().slice"},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.atoms.<slice>.get()"},{"type":"text","value":" where possible; use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.store.get()"},{"type":"text","value":" for full-state/debug reads"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Update TypeScript types to include "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" generic"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Update "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createColumnHelper<TData>()"},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createColumnHelper<TFeatures, TData>()"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TableMeta"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ColumnMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" declaration merging, add the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" generic to your augmentations (optionally, switch to the per-table "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableMeta"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" feature slots)"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"declare module"},{"type":"text","value":" augmentation of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FilterFns"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SortFns"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":" with registry-slot registration, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FilterMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" augmentation with the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filterMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" slot"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(Optional) Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions()"},{"type":"text","value":" for composable configurations"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(Optional) Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" for reusable table patterns"}]}],"checked":false}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check out these examples to see v9 patterns in action:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/basic-inject-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic (Inject Table)"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/basic-app-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic (App Table)"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/filters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Filters"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/column-ordering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Ordering"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/column-pinning","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Pinning"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/column-visibility","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Visibility"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/expanding","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expanding"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/grouping","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grouping"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/row-selection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row Selection"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/composable-tables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Composable Tables"}]}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"what-s-new-in-tanstack-table-v9","text":"What's New in TanStack Table V9","level":2},{"id":"1-better-performance","text":"1. Better Performance","level":3},{"id":"2-state-management-overhaul","text":"2. State Management Overhaul","level":3},{"id":"3-type-safety-improvements","text":"3. Type-Safety Improvements","level":3},{"id":"4-tree-shaking-and-extensibility","text":"4. Tree Shaking and Extensibility","level":3},{"id":"5-composability","text":"5. Composability","level":3},{"id":"6-new-and-refreshed-features","text":"6. New and Refreshed Features","level":3},{"id":"7-modern-builds","text":"7. Modern Builds","level":3},{"id":"the-good-news-most-upgrades-are-opt-in","text":"The Good News: Most Upgrades Are Opt-in","level":3},{"id":"core-breaking-changes","text":"Core Breaking Changes","level":2},{"id":"entrypoint-change","text":"Entrypoint Change","level":3},{"id":"new-required-features-table-option","text":"New Required features Table Option","level":3},{"id":"shortcut-use-stockfeatures-for-table-v8-like-behavior","text":"Shortcut: Use stockFeatures for Table V8-like Behavior","level":4},{"id":"available-features","text":"Available Features","level":4},{"id":"row-model-factories","text":"Row Model Factories","level":3},{"id":"migration-mapping","text":"Migration Mapping","level":4},{"id":"key-change-row-model-factories-and-fn-registries-move-into-tablefeatures","text":"Key Change: Row Model Factories and Fn Registries Move into tableFeatures","level":4},{"id":"full-migration-example","text":"Full Migration Example","level":4},{"id":"prefer-individual-fn-imports-over-full-registries","text":"Prefer Individual Fn Imports Over Full Registries","level":4},{"id":"instance-methods-must-be-called-on-their-instance","text":"Instance Methods Must Be Called on Their Instance","level":3},{"id":"state-management-changes","text":"State Management Changes","level":2},{"id":"accessing-state","text":"Accessing State","level":3},{"id":"optimizing-reads-with-angular-signals","text":"Optimizing Reads with Angular Signals","level":3},{"id":"option-1-read-table-atoms-directly","text":"Option 1: Read table atoms directly","level":4},{"id":"option-2-use-computed-for-selected-object-slices","text":"Option 2: Use computed(...) for selected object slices","level":4},{"id":"controlled-state","text":"Controlled State","level":3},{"id":"feature-by-feature-breaking-changes","text":"Feature-by-Feature Breaking Changes","level":2},{"id":"sorting","text":"Sorting","level":3},{"id":"column-pinning","text":"Column Pinning","level":3},{"id":"column-sizing-vs-column-resizing-split","text":"Column Sizing vs. Column Resizing Split","level":3},{"id":"grouping-and-aggregation","text":"Grouping and Aggregation","level":3},{"id":"row-selection","text":"Row Selection","level":3},{"id":"row-and-internal-api-changes","text":"Row and Internal API Changes","level":3},{"id":"column-helper-changes","text":"Column Helper Changes","level":2},{"id":"new-columns-helper-method","text":"New columns() Helper Method","level":3},{"id":"using-with-createtablehook","text":"Using with createTableHook","level":3},{"id":"rendering-changes","text":"Rendering Changes","level":2},{"id":"flexrender","text":"FlexRender","level":3},{"id":"structural-directive-rendering","text":"Structural directive rendering","level":4},{"id":"shorthand-directives","text":"Shorthand directives","level":4},{"id":"di-aware-render-functions-context-injection","text":"DI-aware render functions + context injection","level":4},{"id":"component-rendering-helper-flexrendercomponent","text":"Component rendering helper: flexRenderComponent","level":4},{"id":"the-tableoptions-utility","text":"The tableOptions() Utility","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic Usage","level":3},{"id":"composing-partial-options","text":"Composing Partial Options","level":3},{"id":"using-with-createtablehook-2","text":"Using with createTableHook","level":3},{"id":"createtablehook-composable-table-patterns","text":"createTableHook: Composable Table Patterns","level":2},{"id":"typescript-changes-summary","text":"TypeScript Changes Summary","level":2},{"id":"type-generics","text":"Type Generics","level":3},{"id":"using-typeof-features","text":"Using typeof features","level":3},{"id":"using-stockfeatures","text":"Using StockFeatures","level":3},{"id":"tablemeta-columnmeta-typing-changes","text":"TableMeta/ColumnMeta Typing Changes","level":3},{"id":"filterfns-sortfns-aggregationfns-filtermeta-augmentation-replaced-by-registry-slots","text":"FilterFns/SortFns/AggregationFns/FilterMeta Augmentation Replaced by Registry Slots","level":3},{"id":"rowdata-type-restriction","text":"RowData Type Restriction","level":3},{"id":"migration-checklist","text":"Migration Checklist","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## What's New in TanStack Table V9\n\nTanStack Table V9 delivers major performance improvements, hundreds of bug fixes, new and refreshed features, and optional helpers for composing and managing tables. Despite the scale of the release, the headless model, core table logic, column definitions, and rendering patterns remain familiar. Here are the key changes:\n\n### 1. Better Performance\n\n- **Lower memory usage**: The core architecture now shares more behavior across table objects, with some large-table scenarios seeing up to 90% memory savings.\n- **Faster client-side row models**: Sorting, filtering, and aggregation paths have improved algorithms and memoization, with many scenarios seeing up to 40-70% speed improvements.\n- **Better column resizing performance**: The same architectural and memoization work also speeds up column resizing.\n\n### 2. State Management Overhaul\n\n- **TanStack Store foundation**: The internal state system has been rebuilt on [TanStack Store](https://tanstack.com/store), providing a reactive, framework-agnostic foundation.\n- **Angular signal integration**: Table atoms are backed by signals. Use `computed(...)` when you want selector-style derivation or custom equality, and keep reads scoped to the state you actually need.\n- **External state remains supported**: You can still use `state` plus `on[State]Change` by owning slices with Angular signals.\n\n### 3. Type-Safety Improvements\n\n- **New and revamped type helpers**: There are helpers for defining columns, custom filters, sorts, aggregations, column and table meta, shared table options and components, and more.\n- **Per-table meta types**: `tableMeta`, `columnMeta`, and `filterMeta` slots let you type meta for a specific table instead of globally augmenting shared interfaces. **No more global declaration merging required!**\n- **Feature-gated APIs**: APIs only exist when their feature is registered, and `tableFeatures()` validates feature prerequisites at the type level.\n\n### 4. Tree Shaking and Extensibility\n\n- **Import only the features you use**: Tables that only need sorting do not ship filtering, pagination, or other unused feature code.\n- **Tree-shakeable row models and functions**: Row model factories and `filterFns` / `sortFns` / `aggregationFns` now live on `tableFeatures()`, so unused processing code can be dropped.\n- **Custom features use the same system**: Your own feature plugins can register state, options, and APIs alongside the built-in features. See the [Custom Features Guide](./custom-features.md).\n\n### 5. Composability\n\n- **`tableOptions`**: Compose reusable table configuration, including features, row models, and default options.\n- **`createTableHook`**: Create reusable, strongly typed Angular table factories with pre-bound features, row models, default options, and component registries.\n\n### 6. New and Refreshed Features\n\n- **New Features**\n  - **Cell Selection**: `cellSelectionFeature` adds spreadsheet-style rectangular cell range selection, with drag, Shift-extend, and multiple disjoint ranges. See the [Cell Selection Guide](./cell-selection.md).\n  - **Cell Spanning**: `cellSpanningFeature` merges body cells across rows and columns (`spanRows` / `spanColumns`, with span-aware cell selection), and header groups now compute `header.rowSpan` so shallow columns can span header rows. See the [Cell Spanning Guide](./cell-spanning.md).\n- **Refreshed Features**\n  - **More capable features**: Aggregation, Row Selection, Column Pinning, and Column Resizing have all been made more feature rich (multiple aggregation definitions per column, Shift range selection, logical `start`/`end` pinning, and more).\n  - **New core APIs**: New table and row APIs (like `table.getMaxSubRowDepth()`, `row.getDisplayIndex()`) round out the core feature set.\n\n### 7. Modern Builds\n\n- **ESM-only**: UMD and CJS builds have been dropped. Packages ship as modern ESM.\n- **TypeScript target `ES2022`**: Compiled output now targets ES2022.\n- **Smaller install size**: Published packages no longer ship `src` or source maps, which reduces install footprint.\n\n### The Good News: Most Upgrades Are Opt-in\n\nWhile v9 is a significant upgrade, **you don't have to adopt everything at once**:\n\n- **Don't want to think about tree-shaking yet?** You can start with `stockFeatures` to include most commonly used features.\n- **Your table markup is largely unchanged.** How you render `<table>`, `<thead>`, `<tr>`, `<td>`, etc. remains the same.\n\nThe main change is **how you define a table** with the Angular adapter, specifically the new `features` option and how row model factories are registered inside it.\n\n## Core Breaking Changes\n\n### Entrypoint Change\n\nThe Angular adapter entrypoint to create a table instance is `injectTable`:\n\n```ts\n// v8\nimport { createAngularTable } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst v8Table = createAngularTable(() => ({\n  // options\n}))\n\n// v9\nimport { injectTable } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst v9Table = injectTable(() => ({\n  // options\n}))\n```\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> `injectTable` evaluates your initializer whenever any Angular signal read inside of it changes.\n> Keep expensive/static values (like `columns` and `features`) as stable references outside the initializer.\n\n### New Required `features` Table Option\n\nIn Table V9, you must explicitly declare which features your table uses. Features, Row Models, and Row Model processing \"Fns\" are defined on the new `features` table option.\n\nIn Table V8, all features were bundled and included in the table setup. In Table V9, you import only what you need.\n\n```ts\n// Table V8\nimport {\n  createAngularTable,\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  sortingFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst v8Table = createAngularTable(() => ({\n  columns,\n  data: data(),\n  getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n  getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(),\n  sortingFns,\n}))\n\n// Table V9\nimport {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  injectTable,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\n// All table options that concern including code modules (features, row models, Fns, etc.)\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature, // new - import and pass the feature you want to use\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(), // now row models are defined on the features object\n  sortFns, // now Fns are defined on the features object\n  // ...more features, row models, etc.\n})\n\n// Define stable references outside the initializer\nconst v9Table = injectTable(() => ({\n  features, // new required option\n  columns: this.columns,\n  data: this.data(),\n}))\n```\n\n#### Shortcut: Use `stockFeatures` for Table V8-like Behavior\n\nIf you want all features without thinking about it (like Table V8), import `stockFeatures`:\n\n```ts\nimport { injectTable, stockFeatures } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features: stockFeatures, // All features included - just like Table V8\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n#### Available Features\n\n| Feature           | Import Name               |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------- |\n| Column Faceting   | `columnFacetingFeature`   |\n| Column Filtering  | `columnFilteringFeature`  |\n| Column Grouping   | `columnGroupingFeature`   |\n| Column Ordering   | `columnOrderingFeature`   |\n| Column Pinning    | `columnPinningFeature`    |\n| Column Resizing   | `columnResizingFeature`   |\n| Column Sizing     | `columnSizingFeature`     |\n| Column Visibility | `columnVisibilityFeature` |\n| Global Filtering  | `globalFilteringFeature`  |\n| Row Aggregation   | `rowAggregationFeature`   |\n| Row Expanding     | `rowExpandingFeature`     |\n| Row Pagination    | `rowPaginationFeature`    |\n| Row Pinning       | `rowPinningFeature`       |\n| Row Selection     | `rowSelectionFeature`     |\n| Row Sorting       | `rowSortingFeature`       |\n\n### Row Model Factories\n\nRow models are the functions that process your data (filtering, sorting, pagination, etc.). In Table V9, row model factories and their `*Fns` registries move from a separate `rowModels` option into `tableFeatures`. Row model slots are type-checked, so each row model must be specified after its associated feature in the same `tableFeatures` call.\n\n#### Migration Mapping\n\n| Table V8 Option            | Table V9 `tableFeatures` Slot | Table V9 Factory Function     |\n| -------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `getCoreRowModel()`        | (automatic)                   | Not needed, always included   |\n| `getFilteredRowModel()`    | `filteredRowModel`            | `createFilteredRowModel()`    |\n| `getSortedRowModel()`      | `sortedRowModel`              | `createSortedRowModel()`      |\n| `getPaginationRowModel()`  | `paginatedRowModel`           | `createPaginatedRowModel()`   |\n| `getExpandedRowModel()`    | `expandedRowModel`            | `createExpandedRowModel()`    |\n| `getGroupedRowModel()`     | `groupedRowModel`             | `createGroupedRowModel()`     |\n| `getFacetedRowModel()`     | `facetedRowModel`             | `createFacetedRowModel()`     |\n| `getFacetedMinMaxValues()` | `facetedMinMaxValues`         | `createFacetedMinMaxValues()` |\n| `getFacetedUniqueValues()` | `facetedUniqueValues`         | `createFacetedUniqueValues()` |\n\nThe `filterFns`, `sortFns`, and `aggregationFns` objects are now registered as named slots on `tableFeatures` rather than passed as arguments to the factory functions.\n\n#### Key Change: Row Model Factories and Fn Registries Move into `tableFeatures`\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  tableFeatures,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createGroupedRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  filterFns, // Built-in filter functions\n  sortFns, // Built-in sort functions\n  aggregationFns, // Built-in aggregation functions\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  columnGroupingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  groupedRowModel: createGroupedRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n  aggregationFns,\n})\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n#### Full Migration Example\n\n```ts\n// v8\nimport {\n  createAngularTable,\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getFilteredRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  getPaginationRowModel,\n  filterFns,\n  sortingFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst v8Table = createAngularTable(() => ({\n  columns,\n  data: data(),\n  getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(), // used to be called \"get*RowModel()\"\n  getFilteredRowModel: getFilteredRowModel(),\n  getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(),\n  getPaginationRowModel: getPaginationRowModel(),\n  filterFns, // used to be passed in as a root option\n  sortingFns,\n}))\n\n// v9\nimport {\n  injectTable,\n  tableFeatures,\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst v9Table = injectTable(() => ({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data: data(),\n}))\n```\n\n#### Prefer Individual Fn Imports Over Full Registries\n\nThe `filterFns`, `sortFns`, and `aggregationFns` registry exports are now deprecated in favor of importing individual `filterFn_*`, `sortFn_*`, and `aggregationFn_*` functions and registering only the ones you use (or passing functions directly in column definitions with no registration at all). The full registries still work, but spreading them puts every built-in function in your bundle. String names, including the default `'auto'`, only resolve functions you have registered.\n\n```ts\n// Before: registers every built-in function\nimport { filterFns, sortFns } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  // ...other features and row models\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n})\n\n// After: registers only the functions you use\nimport {\n  filterFn_includesString,\n  sortFn_alphanumeric,\n  sortFn_text,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  // ...other features and row models\n  filterFns: { includesString: filterFn_includesString },\n  sortFns: { alphanumeric: sortFn_alphanumeric, text: sortFn_text },\n})\n```\n\n### Instance Methods Must Be Called on Their Instance\n\nIn v9, methods on rows, cells, columns, headers, and similar table objects are shared on the object's prototype instead of being created as arrow functions on each object. This improves memory usage, but it means destructuring those methods loses the `this` context they need to operate on the instance.\n\n```ts\n// v8 - worked because getValue closed over the row object\nconst { getValue } = row\nconst value = getValue('name')\n\n// v9 - call the method on the instance\nconst value = row.getValue('name')\n```\n\nThis applies to row, cell, column, header, and related instance APIs, but not to the table instance itself. Audit code that destructures methods from table objects or passes them around as bare callbacks. Prefer calling them through the original object, for example `row.getValue('name')`, `cell.getContext()`, `column.getCanSort()`, or `header.getContext()`.\n\nBecause these methods now live on the prototype, they also do not appear as own properties in `Object.keys(instance)`, object spread, or `JSON.stringify`. A shallow clone like `{ ...row }` copies row data but does not copy row methods. The methods are still callable normally because JavaScript looks them up through the prototype chain.\n\n---\n\n## State Management Changes\n\n### Accessing State\n\nIn v8, you accessed state via `table.getState()`. In v9, read the specific\nstate slice from `table.atoms.<slice>.get()` where possible. Use `table.store.get()`\nwhen you need the full flat state shape, such as debug JSON.\n\n```ts\n// v8\nconst state = table.getState()\nconst v8 = table.getState()\nconst { sorting, pagination } = v8\n\n// v9 - per-slice reads, preferred for Angular render code\nconst sorting = table.atoms.sorting.get()\nconst pagination = table.atoms.pagination.get()\n\n// v9 - full-state flat snapshot\nconst fullState = table.store.get()\nconst v9 = table.store.get()\nconst { sorting: v9Sorting, pagination: v9Pagination } = v9\n```\n\n### Optimizing Reads with Angular Signals\n\nIn Angular, you have a few good options for consuming table state.\n\n#### Option 1: Read table atoms directly\n\nThe Angular adapter backs table atoms with Angular signals. Read the atom you care about directly in templates, effects, or computed values.\n\n```ts\nimport { computed, effect } from '@angular/core'\nimport { shallow } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n\n  // Use computed when deriving from a slice or applying equality.\n  private readonly pagination = computed(\n    () => this.table.atoms.pagination.get(),\n    {\n      equal: shallow,\n    },\n  )\n\n  constructor() {\n    effect(() => {\n      const { pageIndex, pageSize } = this.pagination()\n      console.log('Page', pageIndex, 'Size', pageSize)\n    })\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### Option 2: Use `computed(...)` for selected object slices\n\nUse Angular `computed(...)` when you want selector-style behavior, a derived value, or an equality function. For object/array slices, use `shallow` from `@tanstack/angular-table` to avoid unnecessary downstream work when the slice is recreated with the same values.\n\n```ts\nimport { computed, effect } from '@angular/core'\nimport { shallow } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n\n  // Provide an equality function for object slices\n  readonly pagination = computed(() => this.table.atoms.pagination.get(), {\n    equal: shallow,\n  })\n\n  constructor() {\n    effect(() => {\n      // This effect only re-runs when pagination changes\n      const { pageIndex, pageSize } = this.pagination()\n      console.log('Page', pageIndex, 'Size', pageSize)\n    })\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Controlled State\n\nThe v8-style `state` + `on[State]Change` controlled state patterns still work and remain convenient for simple integrations. For new v9 code, prefer owning state slices with external atoms via the new `atoms` table option (created with `createAtom` from `@tanstack/angular-store`), which give you fine-grained subscriptions without mirroring state through Angular signals. See the [External Atoms section of the Table State Guide](./table-state#external-atoms) and the [Basic External Atoms example](../examples/basic-external-atoms).\n\n```ts\nimport { signal } from '@angular/core'\nimport type { SortingState, PaginationState } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly sorting = signal<SortingState>([])\n  readonly pagination = signal<PaginationState>({ pageIndex: 0, pageSize: 10 })\n\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n    state: {\n      sorting: this.sorting(),\n      pagination: this.pagination(),\n    },\n    onSortingChange: (updater) => {\n      updater instanceof Function\n        ? this.sorting.update(updater)\n        : this.sorting.set(updater)\n    },\n    onPaginationChange: (updater) => {\n      updater instanceof Function\n        ? this.pagination.update(updater)\n        : this.pagination.set(updater)\n    },\n  }))\n}\n```\n\nThe v8-style `onStateChange` callback is no longer part of the v9 table state model. Use per-slice `on[State]Change` callbacks or subscribe to the table store when you need to listen to all state changes.\n\n```ts\nconst unsubscribe = this.table.store.subscribe((state) => {\n  console.log(state)\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## Feature-by-Feature Breaking Changes\n\n### Sorting\n\nSorting-related APIs have been renamed for consistency:\n\n| v8                                | v9                       |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| `sortingFn` (column def option)   | `sortFn`                 |\n| `column.getSortingFn()`           | `column.getSortFn()`     |\n| `column.getAutoSortingFn()`       | `column.getAutoSortFn()` |\n| `SortingFn` type                  | `SortFn` type            |\n| `SortingFns` interface            | `SortFns` interface      |\n| `sortingFns` (built-in functions) | `sortFns`                |\n\nUpdate your column definitions.\n\n### Column Pinning\n\nV9 changes column pinning to use logical `start`/`end` terminology instead of the physical `left`/`right` terminology used in V8. In LTR languages/layouts, `start` usually corresponds to left and `end` to right; in RTL languages/layouts, `start` usually corresponds to right and `end` to left. There are no deprecated aliases.\n\n| V8                                   | V9                                   |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------ |\n| `columnPinning.left`                 | `columnPinning.start`                |\n| `columnPinning.right`                | `columnPinning.end`                  |\n| `column.pin('left')`                 | `column.pin('start')`                |\n| `column.pin('right')`                | `column.pin('end')`                  |\n| `column.getIsPinned() === 'left'`    | `column.getIsPinned() === 'start'`   |\n| `column.getIsPinned() === 'right'`   | `column.getIsPinned() === 'end'`     |\n| `row.getLeftVisibleCells()`          | `row.getStartVisibleCells()`         |\n| `row.getRightVisibleCells()`         | `row.getEndVisibleCells()`           |\n| `table.getLeftHeaderGroups()`        | `table.getStartHeaderGroups()`       |\n| `table.getRightHeaderGroups()`       | `table.getEndHeaderGroups()`         |\n| `table.getLeftLeafColumns()`         | `table.getStartLeafColumns()`        |\n| `table.getRightLeafColumns()`        | `table.getEndLeafColumns()`          |\n| `table.getLeftVisibleLeafColumns()`  | `table.getStartVisibleLeafColumns()` |\n| `table.getRightVisibleLeafColumns()` | `table.getEndVisibleLeafColumns()`   |\n| `table.getLeftTotalSize()`           | `table.getStartTotalSize()`          |\n| `table.getRightTotalSize()`          | `table.getEndTotalSize()`            |\n| `column.getStart('left')`            | `column.getStart('start')`           |\n| `column.getAfter('right')`           | `column.getAfter('end')`             |\n| `column.getIndex('left')`            | `column.getIndex('start')`           |\n| `column.getIndex('right')`           | `column.getIndex('end')`             |\n\nThis rename is about logical table regions, not automatic DOM direction handling. For sticky column pinning, prefer CSS logical properties like `insetInlineStart` and `insetInlineEnd`. The `columnResizeDirection` table option is unchanged.\n\nThe `enablePinning` option has also been split into separate options:\n\n```ts\n// v8\nenablePinning: true\n\n// v9\nenableColumnPinning: true\nenableRowPinning: true\n```\n\n### Column Sizing vs. Column Resizing Split\n\nIn v8, column sizing and resizing were combined in a single feature. In v9, they've been split into separate features for better tree-shaking.\n\n| v8                                | v9                                              |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `ColumnSizing` (combined feature) | `columnSizingFeature` + `columnResizingFeature` |\n| `columnSizingInfo` state          | `columnResizing` state                          |\n| `setColumnSizingInfo()`           | `setColumnResizing()`                           |\n| `onColumnSizingInfoChange` option | `onColumnResizingChange` option                 |\n\nIf you only need column sizing (fixed widths) without interactive resizing, you can import just `columnSizingFeature`. If you need drag-to-resize functionality, import both.\n\n### Grouping and Aggregation\n\nAggregation is now its own feature, independent from column grouping. `stockFeatures` still includes both, so tables using it need no feature-registration change. If you declare features explicitly, add `rowAggregationFeature` whenever columns use `aggregationFn`, `aggregatedCell`, `getAggregationValue`, or `cell.getIsAggregated`. Add `columnGroupingFeature` and `groupedRowModel` only when you also group rows.\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  columnGroupingFeature, // only for grouped rows\n  groupedRowModel: createGroupedRowModel(),\n  aggregationFns: { sum: aggregationFn_sum },\n})\n```\n\nCustom aggregation callables have changed to context-based definitions:\n\n```ts\n// Table V8/earlier V9 betas\nconst total = (columnId, leafRows, childRows) =>\n  leafRows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + row.getValue(columnId), 0)\n\n// Current V9\nconst total = constructAggregationFn({\n  aggregate: ({ rows, getValue }) =>\n    rows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + Number(getValue(row)), 0),\n})\n```\n\nThe old per-function choice between `childRows` and `leafRows` is replaced by a single depth-selected `context.rows`, controlled by the `maxAggregationDepth` column option. The default (`0`) preserves V8's direct-child grouped aggregation; use `Infinity` to aggregate terminal leaf rows.\n\n`column.getAggregationValue()` now takes a single options object instead of positional arguments:\n\n```ts\n// Table V8/earlier V9 betas\ncolumn.getAggregationValue(rows, maxDepth)\n\n// Current V9\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows, maxDepth })\n```\n\n`column.getAggregationFn()` is now `column.getAggregationFns()` because a column can run multiple definitions, and the old callable `AggregationFn`/`CreatedAggregationFn` types are replaced by `AggregationFnDef`.\n\nSee the [Grouping Guide](./grouping) and the [Aggregation Guide](./aggregation) for full documentation of the new capabilities.\n\n### Row Selection\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Minor breaking change:** `row.getToggleSelectedHandler()` now enables inclusive Shift range selection by default when `rowSelectionFeature` is enabled. Existing checkboxes or rows wired through this handler establish an anchor on an ordinary interaction and select or deselect the current display-order range on a Shift interaction. Direct `row.toggleSelected()` calls are unchanged.\n>\n> Set `enableRowRangeSelection: false` to preserve the previous non-range handler behavior. The handler must receive an event that exposes Shift directly or through `nativeEvent`; see [Shift Range Selection](./row-selection.md#shift-range-selection).\n\nThe \"some rows selected\" checks were simplified to mean \"at least one row is selected\":\n\n| API                                 | v8                                                  | v9                                            |\n| ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `table.getIsSomeRowsSelected()`     | `true` when some but not all rows are selected      | `true` when at least one row is selected      |\n| `table.getIsSomePageRowsSelected()` | `true` when some but not all page rows are selected | `true` when at least one page row is selected |\n\nIn v8 these returned `false` once every row was selected; in v9 they stay `true`. If you use them to drive an indeterminate \"select all\" checkbox, gate the indeterminate state on the matching all-selected check so it clears at full selection:\n\n`getIsSomeRowsSelected() && !getIsAllRowsSelected()`\n\n### Row and Internal API Changes\n\nSome row APIs have changed from private to public:\n\n| v8                                       | v9                                     |\n| ---------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `row._getAllCellsByColumnId()` (private) | `row.getAllCellsByColumnId()` (public) |\n\nAll other internal APIs prefixed with `_` have been removed. If you were using any of these, use their public equivalents.\n\n- Removed: `table._getPinnedRows()`\n- Removed: `table._getFacetedRowModel()`\n- Removed: `table._getFacetedMinMaxValues()`\n- Removed: `table._getFacetedUniqueValues()`\n\n---\n\n## Column Helper Changes\n\nThe `createColumnHelper` function now requires a `TFeatures` type parameter in addition to `TData`:\n\n```ts\n// v8\nimport { createColumnHelper } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst columnHelperV8 = createColumnHelper<Person>()\n\n// v9\nimport {\n  createColumnHelper,\n  tableFeatures,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ rowSortingFeature })\nconst columnHelperV9 = createColumnHelper<typeof features, Person>()\n```\n\n### New `columns()` Helper Method\n\nv9 adds a `columns()` helper for better type inference when wrapping column arrays.\n\n```ts\nconst columnHelper = createColumnHelper<typeof features, Person>()\n\n// Wrap your columns array for better type inference\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    header: 'First Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('lastName', {\n    id: 'lastName',\n    header: () => 'Last Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.display({\n    id: 'actions',\n    header: 'Actions',\n    cell: () => 'Edit',\n  }),\n])\n```\n\n### Using with `createTableHook`\n\nWhen using `createTableHook`, you get a pre-bound `createAppColumnHelper` that only requires `TData`:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createTableHook,\n  tableFeatures,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  sortFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst { injectAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({ features })\n\n// TFeatures is already bound, only need TData!\nconst columnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n```\n\n---\n\n## Rendering Changes\n\n### `FlexRender`\n\nThe rendering primitives in the Angular adapter are `FlexRender` and the `*flexRender` directives.\n\nIn v9, you can continue to render header/cell/footer content using the Angular adapter rendering utilities, but there are a few important improvements and helper APIs to be aware of.\n\n#### Structural directive rendering\n\nAngular rendering is directive-based:\n\n- `FlexRender` / `*flexRender` renders arbitrary render content (primitives, `TemplateRef`, component types, or `flexRenderComponent(...)` wrappers)\n- The directive is responsible for mounting embedded views or components via `ViewContainerRef`\n\n#### Shorthand directives\n\nIf you're rendering standard table content, prefer the shorthand helpers:\n\n- `*flexRenderCell=\"cell; let value\"`\n- `*flexRenderHeader=\"header; let value\"`\n- `*flexRenderFooter=\"footer; let value\"`\n\nThese automatically select the correct column definition (`columnDef.cell` / `header` / `footer`) and the right props (`cell.getContext()` / `header.getContext()`), so you don't need to manually provide `props:`.\n\n#### DI-aware render functions + context injection\n\nColumn definition render functions (`header`, `cell`, `footer`) run inside an Angular injection context, so they can safely call `inject()` and use signals.\n\nWhen a component is rendered through the FlexRender directives, you can also access the full render props object via DI using `injectFlexRenderContext()`.\n\n#### Component rendering helper: `flexRenderComponent`\n\nIf you need to render an Angular component with explicit configuration (custom `inputs`, `outputs`, `injector`, and Angular v20+ creation-time `bindings`/`directives`), return a `flexRenderComponent(Component, options)` wrapper from your column definition.\n\nFor complete rendering details (including component rendering, `TemplateRef`, `flexRenderComponent`, and context helpers), see the [FlexRender Guide](./flex-render).\n\n---\n\n## The `tableOptions()` Utility\n\nThe `tableOptions()` helper provides type-safe composition of table options. It's useful for creating reusable partial configurations that can be spread into your table setup.\n\n### Basic Usage\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  injectTable,\n  tableOptions,\n  tableFeatures,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\nimport { isDevMode } from '@angular/core'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ rowSortingFeature })\n\n// Create a reusable options object with features pre-configured\nconst baseOptions = tableOptions({\n  features,\n  debugTable: isDevMode(),\n})\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    ...baseOptions,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n### Composing Partial Options\n\n`tableOptions()` lets you omit required fields (like `data`, `columns`, or `features`) when creating partial configurations:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  tableOptions,\n  tableFeatures,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n  filterFns,\n})\n\n// Partial options without data or columns\nconst featureOptions = tableOptions({ features })\n```\n\n```ts\nimport { injectTable, tableOptions } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\n// Another partial (inherits features from spread)\nconst paginationDefaults = tableOptions({\n  initialState: {\n    pagination: { pageIndex: 0, pageSize: 25 },\n  },\n})\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    ...featureOptions,\n    ...paginationDefaults,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n### Using with `createTableHook`\n\n`tableOptions()` pairs well with `createTableHook` for building composable table factories:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createTableHook,\n  tableOptions,\n  tableFeatures,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  sortFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst sharedOptions = tableOptions({ features })\n\nconst { injectAppTable } = createTableHook(sharedOptions)\n```\n\n---\n\n## `createTableHook`: Composable Table Patterns\n\n**This is an advanced, optional feature.** You don't need to use `createTableHook`; `injectTable` is sufficient for most use cases.\n\nFor applications with multiple tables sharing the same configuration, `createTableHook` lets you define features, row models, and reusable components once.\n\nFor full setup and patterns, see the [Composable Tables Guide](./composable-tables.md).\n\n---\n\n## TypeScript Changes Summary\n\n### Type Generics\n\nMost types now require a `TFeatures` parameter:\n\n```txt\n// v8\ntype Column<TData>\ntype ColumnDef<TData>\ntype Table<TData>\ntype Row<TData>\ntype Cell<TData, TValue>\n\n// v9\ntype Column<TFeatures, TData, TValue>\ntype ColumnDef<TFeatures, TData, TValue>\ntype Table<TFeatures, TData>\ntype Row<TFeatures, TData>\ntype Cell<TFeatures, TData, TValue>\n```\n\n### Using `typeof features`\n\nThe easiest way to get the `TFeatures` type is with `typeof`:\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n})\n\ntype MyFeatures = typeof features\n\nconst columns: ColumnDef<typeof features, Person>[] = [...]\n```\n\n### Using `StockFeatures`\n\nIf using `stockFeatures`, use the `StockFeatures` type:\n\n```ts\nimport type { StockFeatures, ColumnDef } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst columns: ColumnDef<StockFeatures, Person>[] = [...]\n```\n\n### `TableMeta`/`ColumnMeta` Typing Changes\n\nNo more declaration merging required! (Although it still works if you want to keep using it)\n\nGlobal declaration merging to extend `TableMeta` or `ColumnMeta` works exactly like it did in v8. The only change you need to make is updating the generics shape: both interfaces now take `TFeatures` as the first type parameter.\n\nOptionally, v9 also adds a new way to declare meta types **per-table** without declaration merging. You can use type-only `tableMeta`/`columnMeta` slots on the `features` option, which only affect tables created with that `features` object:\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<{ customProperty: string }>(),\n})\n```\n\nSee the new [Table and Column Meta Guide](../../../guide/table-and-column-meta) for full details on both approaches.\n\n### `FilterFns`/`SortFns`/`AggregationFns`/`FilterMeta` Augmentation Replaced by Registry Slots\n\nIn v8, making a custom function usable as a string reference (like `filterFn: 'fuzzy'`) required `declare module` augmentation of the `FilterFns` interface, and typing filter meta required augmenting `FilterMeta`. In v9, registering the function in the matching registry slot does both jobs with no global augmentation:\n\n```ts\n// v8\ndeclare module '@tanstack/angular-table' {\n  interface FilterFns {\n    fuzzy: FilterFn<unknown>\n  }\n  interface FilterMeta {\n    itemRank: RankingInfo\n  }\n}\n\n// v9 - register in the slot; the key becomes a valid string value\ninterface FuzzyFilterMeta {\n  itemRank?: RankingInfo\n}\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  filterFns: { fuzzy: fuzzyFilter },\n  filterMeta: metaHelper<FuzzyFilterMeta>(),\n})\n\n// 'fuzzy' now typechecks in column defs for tables using these features\ncolumnHelper.accessor('name', { filterFn: 'fuzzy' })\n```\n\nThe same pattern applies to `sortFns` (for `sortFn` string values) and `aggregationFns` (for `aggregationFn` string values). See the [Fuzzy Filtering Guide](./fuzzy-filtering.md) for a complete example.\n\n### `RowData` Type Restriction\n\nThe `RowData` type is now more restrictive:\n\n```ts\n// v8 - very permissive\ntype RowData = unknown\n\n// v9 - must be a record or array\ntype RowData = Record<string, any> | Array<any>\n```\n\nThis change improves type safety. If you were passing unusual data types, ensure your data conforms to `Record<string, any>` or `Array<any>`.\n\n---\n\n## Migration Checklist\n\n- [ ] Update your table setup to v9 and define `features` using `tableFeatures()` (or use `stockFeatures`)\n- [ ] Migrate `get*RowModel()` options: move row model factories into `tableFeatures` as named slots\n- [ ] Move `filterFns`, `sortFns`, and `aggregationFns` into `tableFeatures` as named slots (no longer passed as factory arguments)\n- [ ] Replace destructured row/cell/column/header methods with calls on the instance (for example, `row.getValue('name')`)\n- [ ] Rename `sortingFn` → `sortFn` in column definitions\n- [ ] Update column pinning to `start`/`end` terminology (`columnPinning.start`, `column.pin('end')`, `getStart*`/`getEnd*` APIs)\n- [ ] Replace `enablePinning` with `enableColumnPinning`/`enableRowPinning` if used\n- [ ] Rename `columnSizingInfo` state → `columnResizing` (and related options)\n- [ ] Convert custom aggregation callables to `constructAggregationFn({ aggregate, merge? })` definitions\n- [ ] Update state access: `table.getState().slice` → `table.atoms.<slice>.get()` where possible; use `table.store.get()` for full-state/debug reads\n- [ ] Update TypeScript types to include `TFeatures` generic\n- [ ] Update `createColumnHelper<TData>()` → `createColumnHelper<TFeatures, TData>()`\n- [ ] If you use `TableMeta`/`ColumnMeta` declaration merging, add the `TFeatures` generic to your augmentations (optionally, switch to the per-table `tableMeta`/`columnMeta` feature slots)\n- [ ] Replace `declare module` augmentation of `FilterFns`/`SortFns`/`AggregationFns` with registry-slot registration, and `FilterMeta` augmentation with the `filterMeta` slot\n- [ ] (Optional) Use `tableOptions()` for composable configurations\n- [ ] (Optional) Use `createTableHook` for reusable table patterns\n\n---\n\n## Examples\n\nCheck out these examples to see v9 patterns in action:\n\n- [Basic (Inject Table)](../examples/basic-inject-table)\n- [Basic (App Table)](../examples/basic-app-table)\n- [Filters](../examples/filters)\n- [Column Ordering](../examples/column-ordering)\n- [Column Pinning](../examples/column-pinning)\n- [Column Visibility](../examples/column-visibility)\n- [Expanding](../examples/expanding)\n- [Grouping](../examples/grouping)\n- [Row Selection](../examples/row-selection)\n- [Composable Tables](../examples/composable-tables)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Migrating to TanStack Table V9 (Angular)\n---\n\n## What's New in TanStack Table V9\n\nTanStack Table V9 delivers major performance improvements, hundreds of bug fixes, new and refreshed features, and optional helpers for composing and managing tables. Despite the scale of the release, the headless model, core table logic, column definitions, and rendering patterns remain familiar. Here are the key changes:\n\n### 1. Better Performance\n\n- **Lower memory usage**: The core architecture now shares more behavior across table objects, with some large-table scenarios seeing up to 90% memory savings.\n- **Faster client-side row models**: Sorting, filtering, and aggregation paths have improved algorithms and memoization, with many scenarios seeing up to 40-70% speed improvements.\n- **Better column resizing performance**: The same architectural and memoization work also speeds up column resizing.\n\n### 2. State Management Overhaul\n\n- **TanStack Store foundation**: The internal state system has been rebuilt on [TanStack Store](https://tanstack.com/store), providing a reactive, framework-agnostic foundation.\n- **Angular signal integration**: Table atoms are backed by signals. Use `computed(...)` when you want selector-style derivation or custom equality, and keep reads scoped to the state you actually need.\n- **External state remains supported**: You can still use `state` plus `on[State]Change` by owning slices with Angular signals.\n\n### 3. Type-Safety Improvements\n\n- **New and revamped type helpers**: There are helpers for defining columns, custom filters, sorts, aggregations, column and table meta, shared table options and components, and more.\n- **Per-table meta types**: `tableMeta`, `columnMeta`, and `filterMeta` slots let you type meta for a specific table instead of globally augmenting shared interfaces. **No more global declaration merging required!**\n- **Feature-gated APIs**: APIs only exist when their feature is registered, and `tableFeatures()` validates feature prerequisites at the type level.\n\n### 4. Tree Shaking and Extensibility\n\n- **Import only the features you use**: Tables that only need sorting do not ship filtering, pagination, or other unused feature code.\n- **Tree-shakeable row models and functions**: Row model factories and `filterFns` / `sortFns` / `aggregationFns` now live on `tableFeatures()`, so unused processing code can be dropped.\n- **Custom features use the same system**: Your own feature plugins can register state, options, and APIs alongside the built-in features. See the [Custom Features Guide](./custom-features.md).\n\n### 5. Composability\n\n- **`tableOptions`**: Compose reusable table configuration, including features, row models, and default options.\n- **`createTableHook`**: Create reusable, strongly typed Angular table factories with pre-bound features, row models, default options, and component registries.\n\n### 6. New and Refreshed Features\n\n- **New Features**\n  - **Cell Selection**: `cellSelectionFeature` adds spreadsheet-style rectangular cell range selection, with drag, Shift-extend, and multiple disjoint ranges. See the [Cell Selection Guide](./cell-selection.md).\n  - **Cell Spanning**: `cellSpanningFeature` merges body cells across rows and columns (`spanRows` / `spanColumns`, with span-aware cell selection), and header groups now compute `header.rowSpan` so shallow columns can span header rows. See the [Cell Spanning Guide](./cell-spanning.md).\n- **Refreshed Features**\n  - **More capable features**: Aggregation, Row Selection, Column Pinning, and Column Resizing have all been made more feature rich (multiple aggregation definitions per column, Shift range selection, logical `start`/`end` pinning, and more).\n  - **New core APIs**: New table and row APIs (like `table.getMaxSubRowDepth()`, `row.getDisplayIndex()`) round out the core feature set.\n\n### 7. Modern Builds\n\n- **ESM-only**: UMD and CJS builds have been dropped. Packages ship as modern ESM.\n- **TypeScript target `ES2022`**: Compiled output now targets ES2022.\n- **Smaller install size**: Published packages no longer ship `src` or source maps, which reduces install footprint.\n\n### The Good News: Most Upgrades Are Opt-in\n\nWhile v9 is a significant upgrade, **you don't have to adopt everything at once**:\n\n- **Don't want to think about tree-shaking yet?** You can start with `stockFeatures` to include most commonly used features.\n- **Your table markup is largely unchanged.** How you render `<table>`, `<thead>`, `<tr>`, `<td>`, etc. remains the same.\n\nThe main change is **how you define a table** with the Angular adapter, specifically the new `features` option and how row model factories are registered inside it.\n\n## Core Breaking Changes\n\n### Entrypoint Change\n\nThe Angular adapter entrypoint to create a table instance is `injectTable`:\n\n```ts\n// v8\nimport { createAngularTable } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst v8Table = createAngularTable(() => ({\n  // options\n}))\n\n// v9\nimport { injectTable } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst v9Table = injectTable(() => ({\n  // options\n}))\n```\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> `injectTable` evaluates your initializer whenever any Angular signal read inside of it changes.\n> Keep expensive/static values (like `columns` and `features`) as stable references outside the initializer.\n\n### New Required `features` Table Option\n\nIn Table V9, you must explicitly declare which features your table uses. Features, Row Models, and Row Model processing \"Fns\" are defined on the new `features` table option.\n\nIn Table V8, all features were bundled and included in the table setup. In Table V9, you import only what you need.\n\n```ts\n// Table V8\nimport {\n  createAngularTable,\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  sortingFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst v8Table = createAngularTable(() => ({\n  columns,\n  data: data(),\n  getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(),\n  getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(),\n  sortingFns,\n}))\n\n// Table V9\nimport {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  injectTable,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\n// All table options that concern including code modules (features, row models, Fns, etc.)\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature, // new - import and pass the feature you want to use\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(), // now row models are defined on the features object\n  sortFns, // now Fns are defined on the features object\n  // ...more features, row models, etc.\n})\n\n// Define stable references outside the initializer\nconst v9Table = injectTable(() => ({\n  features, // new required option\n  columns: this.columns,\n  data: this.data(),\n}))\n```\n\n#### Shortcut: Use `stockFeatures` for Table V8-like Behavior\n\nIf you want all features without thinking about it (like Table V8), import `stockFeatures`:\n\n```ts\nimport { injectTable, stockFeatures } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features: stockFeatures, // All features included - just like Table V8\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n#### Available Features\n\n| Feature           | Import Name               |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------- |\n| Column Faceting   | `columnFacetingFeature`   |\n| Column Filtering  | `columnFilteringFeature`  |\n| Column Grouping   | `columnGroupingFeature`   |\n| Column Ordering   | `columnOrderingFeature`   |\n| Column Pinning    | `columnPinningFeature`    |\n| Column Resizing   | `columnResizingFeature`   |\n| Column Sizing     | `columnSizingFeature`     |\n| Column Visibility | `columnVisibilityFeature` |\n| Global Filtering  | `globalFilteringFeature`  |\n| Row Aggregation   | `rowAggregationFeature`   |\n| Row Expanding     | `rowExpandingFeature`     |\n| Row Pagination    | `rowPaginationFeature`    |\n| Row Pinning       | `rowPinningFeature`       |\n| Row Selection     | `rowSelectionFeature`     |\n| Row Sorting       | `rowSortingFeature`       |\n\n### Row Model Factories\n\nRow models are the functions that process your data (filtering, sorting, pagination, etc.). In Table V9, row model factories and their `*Fns` registries move from a separate `rowModels` option into `tableFeatures`. Row model slots are type-checked, so each row model must be specified after its associated feature in the same `tableFeatures` call.\n\n#### Migration Mapping\n\n| Table V8 Option            | Table V9 `tableFeatures` Slot | Table V9 Factory Function     |\n| -------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `getCoreRowModel()`        | (automatic)                   | Not needed, always included   |\n| `getFilteredRowModel()`    | `filteredRowModel`            | `createFilteredRowModel()`    |\n| `getSortedRowModel()`      | `sortedRowModel`              | `createSortedRowModel()`      |\n| `getPaginationRowModel()`  | `paginatedRowModel`           | `createPaginatedRowModel()`   |\n| `getExpandedRowModel()`    | `expandedRowModel`            | `createExpandedRowModel()`    |\n| `getGroupedRowModel()`     | `groupedRowModel`             | `createGroupedRowModel()`     |\n| `getFacetedRowModel()`     | `facetedRowModel`             | `createFacetedRowModel()`     |\n| `getFacetedMinMaxValues()` | `facetedMinMaxValues`         | `createFacetedMinMaxValues()` |\n| `getFacetedUniqueValues()` | `facetedUniqueValues`         | `createFacetedUniqueValues()` |\n\nThe `filterFns`, `sortFns`, and `aggregationFns` objects are now registered as named slots on `tableFeatures` rather than passed as arguments to the factory functions.\n\n#### Key Change: Row Model Factories and Fn Registries Move into `tableFeatures`\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  tableFeatures,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createGroupedRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  filterFns, // Built-in filter functions\n  sortFns, // Built-in sort functions\n  aggregationFns, // Built-in aggregation functions\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  columnGroupingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  groupedRowModel: createGroupedRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n  aggregationFns,\n})\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n#### Full Migration Example\n\n```ts\n// v8\nimport {\n  createAngularTable,\n  getCoreRowModel,\n  getFilteredRowModel,\n  getSortedRowModel,\n  getPaginationRowModel,\n  filterFns,\n  sortingFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst v8Table = createAngularTable(() => ({\n  columns,\n  data: data(),\n  getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel(), // used to be called \"get*RowModel()\"\n  getFilteredRowModel: getFilteredRowModel(),\n  getSortedRowModel: getSortedRowModel(),\n  getPaginationRowModel: getPaginationRowModel(),\n  filterFns, // used to be passed in as a root option\n  sortingFns,\n}))\n\n// v9\nimport {\n  injectTable,\n  tableFeatures,\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst v9Table = injectTable(() => ({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data: data(),\n}))\n```\n\n#### Prefer Individual Fn Imports Over Full Registries\n\nThe `filterFns`, `sortFns`, and `aggregationFns` registry exports are now deprecated in favor of importing individual `filterFn_*`, `sortFn_*`, and `aggregationFn_*` functions and registering only the ones you use (or passing functions directly in column definitions with no registration at all). The full registries still work, but spreading them puts every built-in function in your bundle. String names, including the default `'auto'`, only resolve functions you have registered.\n\n```ts\n// Before: registers every built-in function\nimport { filterFns, sortFns } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  // ...other features and row models\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n})\n\n// After: registers only the functions you use\nimport {\n  filterFn_includesString,\n  sortFn_alphanumeric,\n  sortFn_text,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  // ...other features and row models\n  filterFns: { includesString: filterFn_includesString },\n  sortFns: { alphanumeric: sortFn_alphanumeric, text: sortFn_text },\n})\n```\n\n### Instance Methods Must Be Called on Their Instance\n\nIn v9, methods on rows, cells, columns, headers, and similar table objects are shared on the object's prototype instead of being created as arrow functions on each object. This improves memory usage, but it means destructuring those methods loses the `this` context they need to operate on the instance.\n\n```ts\n// v8 - worked because getValue closed over the row object\nconst { getValue } = row\nconst value = getValue('name')\n\n// v9 - call the method on the instance\nconst value = row.getValue('name')\n```\n\nThis applies to row, cell, column, header, and related instance APIs, but not to the table instance itself. Audit code that destructures methods from table objects or passes them around as bare callbacks. Prefer calling them through the original object, for example `row.getValue('name')`, `cell.getContext()`, `column.getCanSort()`, or `header.getContext()`.\n\nBecause these methods now live on the prototype, they also do not appear as own properties in `Object.keys(instance)`, object spread, or `JSON.stringify`. A shallow clone like `{ ...row }` copies row data but does not copy row methods. The methods are still callable normally because JavaScript looks them up through the prototype chain.\n\n---\n\n## State Management Changes\n\n### Accessing State\n\nIn v8, you accessed state via `table.getState()`. In v9, read the specific\nstate slice from `table.atoms.<slice>.get()` where possible. Use `table.store.get()`\nwhen you need the full flat state shape, such as debug JSON.\n\n```ts\n// v8\nconst state = table.getState()\nconst v8 = table.getState()\nconst { sorting, pagination } = v8\n\n// v9 - per-slice reads, preferred for Angular render code\nconst sorting = table.atoms.sorting.get()\nconst pagination = table.atoms.pagination.get()\n\n// v9 - full-state flat snapshot\nconst fullState = table.store.get()\nconst v9 = table.store.get()\nconst { sorting: v9Sorting, pagination: v9Pagination } = v9\n```\n\n### Optimizing Reads with Angular Signals\n\nIn Angular, you have a few good options for consuming table state.\n\n#### Option 1: Read table atoms directly\n\nThe Angular adapter backs table atoms with Angular signals. Read the atom you care about directly in templates, effects, or computed values.\n\n```ts\nimport { computed, effect } from '@angular/core'\nimport { shallow } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n\n  // Use computed when deriving from a slice or applying equality.\n  private readonly pagination = computed(\n    () => this.table.atoms.pagination.get(),\n    {\n      equal: shallow,\n    },\n  )\n\n  constructor() {\n    effect(() => {\n      const { pageIndex, pageSize } = this.pagination()\n      console.log('Page', pageIndex, 'Size', pageSize)\n    })\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### Option 2: Use `computed(...)` for selected object slices\n\nUse Angular `computed(...)` when you want selector-style behavior, a derived value, or an equality function. For object/array slices, use `shallow` from `@tanstack/angular-table` to avoid unnecessary downstream work when the slice is recreated with the same values.\n\n```ts\nimport { computed, effect } from '@angular/core'\nimport { shallow } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n\n  // Provide an equality function for object slices\n  readonly pagination = computed(() => this.table.atoms.pagination.get(), {\n    equal: shallow,\n  })\n\n  constructor() {\n    effect(() => {\n      // This effect only re-runs when pagination changes\n      const { pageIndex, pageSize } = this.pagination()\n      console.log('Page', pageIndex, 'Size', pageSize)\n    })\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Controlled State\n\nThe v8-style `state` + `on[State]Change` controlled state patterns still work and remain convenient for simple integrations. For new v9 code, prefer owning state slices with external atoms via the new `atoms` table option (created with `createAtom` from `@tanstack/angular-store`), which give you fine-grained subscriptions without mirroring state through Angular signals. See the [External Atoms section of the Table State Guide](./table-state#external-atoms) and the [Basic External Atoms example](../examples/basic-external-atoms).\n\n```ts\nimport { signal } from '@angular/core'\nimport type { SortingState, PaginationState } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly sorting = signal<SortingState>([])\n  readonly pagination = signal<PaginationState>({ pageIndex: 0, pageSize: 10 })\n\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n    state: {\n      sorting: this.sorting(),\n      pagination: this.pagination(),\n    },\n    onSortingChange: (updater) => {\n      updater instanceof Function\n        ? this.sorting.update(updater)\n        : this.sorting.set(updater)\n    },\n    onPaginationChange: (updater) => {\n      updater instanceof Function\n        ? this.pagination.update(updater)\n        : this.pagination.set(updater)\n    },\n  }))\n}\n```\n\nThe v8-style `onStateChange` callback is no longer part of the v9 table state model. Use per-slice `on[State]Change` callbacks or subscribe to the table store when you need to listen to all state changes.\n\n```ts\nconst unsubscribe = this.table.store.subscribe((state) => {\n  console.log(state)\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## Feature-by-Feature Breaking Changes\n\n### Sorting\n\nSorting-related APIs have been renamed for consistency:\n\n| v8                                | v9                       |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| `sortingFn` (column def option)   | `sortFn`                 |\n| `column.getSortingFn()`           | `column.getSortFn()`     |\n| `column.getAutoSortingFn()`       | `column.getAutoSortFn()` |\n| `SortingFn` type                  | `SortFn` type            |\n| `SortingFns` interface            | `SortFns` interface      |\n| `sortingFns` (built-in functions) | `sortFns`                |\n\nUpdate your column definitions.\n\n### Column Pinning\n\nV9 changes column pinning to use logical `start`/`end` terminology instead of the physical `left`/`right` terminology used in V8. In LTR languages/layouts, `start` usually corresponds to left and `end` to right; in RTL languages/layouts, `start` usually corresponds to right and `end` to left. There are no deprecated aliases.\n\n| V8                                   | V9                                   |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------ |\n| `columnPinning.left`                 | `columnPinning.start`                |\n| `columnPinning.right`                | `columnPinning.end`                  |\n| `column.pin('left')`                 | `column.pin('start')`                |\n| `column.pin('right')`                | `column.pin('end')`                  |\n| `column.getIsPinned() === 'left'`    | `column.getIsPinned() === 'start'`   |\n| `column.getIsPinned() === 'right'`   | `column.getIsPinned() === 'end'`     |\n| `row.getLeftVisibleCells()`          | `row.getStartVisibleCells()`         |\n| `row.getRightVisibleCells()`         | `row.getEndVisibleCells()`           |\n| `table.getLeftHeaderGroups()`        | `table.getStartHeaderGroups()`       |\n| `table.getRightHeaderGroups()`       | `table.getEndHeaderGroups()`         |\n| `table.getLeftLeafColumns()`         | `table.getStartLeafColumns()`        |\n| `table.getRightLeafColumns()`        | `table.getEndLeafColumns()`          |\n| `table.getLeftVisibleLeafColumns()`  | `table.getStartVisibleLeafColumns()` |\n| `table.getRightVisibleLeafColumns()` | `table.getEndVisibleLeafColumns()`   |\n| `table.getLeftTotalSize()`           | `table.getStartTotalSize()`          |\n| `table.getRightTotalSize()`          | `table.getEndTotalSize()`            |\n| `column.getStart('left')`            | `column.getStart('start')`           |\n| `column.getAfter('right')`           | `column.getAfter('end')`             |\n| `column.getIndex('left')`            | `column.getIndex('start')`           |\n| `column.getIndex('right')`           | `column.getIndex('end')`             |\n\nThis rename is about logical table regions, not automatic DOM direction handling. For sticky column pinning, prefer CSS logical properties like `insetInlineStart` and `insetInlineEnd`. The `columnResizeDirection` table option is unchanged.\n\nThe `enablePinning` option has also been split into separate options:\n\n```ts\n// v8\nenablePinning: true\n\n// v9\nenableColumnPinning: true\nenableRowPinning: true\n```\n\n### Column Sizing vs. Column Resizing Split\n\nIn v8, column sizing and resizing were combined in a single feature. In v9, they've been split into separate features for better tree-shaking.\n\n| v8                                | v9                                              |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `ColumnSizing` (combined feature) | `columnSizingFeature` + `columnResizingFeature` |\n| `columnSizingInfo` state          | `columnResizing` state                          |\n| `setColumnSizingInfo()`           | `setColumnResizing()`                           |\n| `onColumnSizingInfoChange` option | `onColumnResizingChange` option                 |\n\nIf you only need column sizing (fixed widths) without interactive resizing, you can import just `columnSizingFeature`. If you need drag-to-resize functionality, import both.\n\n### Grouping and Aggregation\n\nAggregation is now its own feature, independent from column grouping. `stockFeatures` still includes both, so tables using it need no feature-registration change. If you declare features explicitly, add `rowAggregationFeature` whenever columns use `aggregationFn`, `aggregatedCell`, `getAggregationValue`, or `cell.getIsAggregated`. Add `columnGroupingFeature` and `groupedRowModel` only when you also group rows.\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  columnGroupingFeature, // only for grouped rows\n  groupedRowModel: createGroupedRowModel(),\n  aggregationFns: { sum: aggregationFn_sum },\n})\n```\n\nCustom aggregation callables have changed to context-based definitions:\n\n```ts\n// Table V8/earlier V9 betas\nconst total = (columnId, leafRows, childRows) =>\n  leafRows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + row.getValue(columnId), 0)\n\n// Current V9\nconst total = constructAggregationFn({\n  aggregate: ({ rows, getValue }) =>\n    rows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + Number(getValue(row)), 0),\n})\n```\n\nThe old per-function choice between `childRows` and `leafRows` is replaced by a single depth-selected `context.rows`, controlled by the `maxAggregationDepth` column option. The default (`0`) preserves V8's direct-child grouped aggregation; use `Infinity` to aggregate terminal leaf rows.\n\n`column.getAggregationValue()` now takes a single options object instead of positional arguments:\n\n```ts\n// Table V8/earlier V9 betas\ncolumn.getAggregationValue(rows, maxDepth)\n\n// Current V9\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows, maxDepth })\n```\n\n`column.getAggregationFn()` is now `column.getAggregationFns()` because a column can run multiple definitions, and the old callable `AggregationFn`/`CreatedAggregationFn` types are replaced by `AggregationFnDef`.\n\nSee the [Grouping Guide](./grouping) and the [Aggregation Guide](./aggregation) for full documentation of the new capabilities.\n\n### Row Selection\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Minor breaking change:** `row.getToggleSelectedHandler()` now enables inclusive Shift range selection by default when `rowSelectionFeature` is enabled. Existing checkboxes or rows wired through this handler establish an anchor on an ordinary interaction and select or deselect the current display-order range on a Shift interaction. Direct `row.toggleSelected()` calls are unchanged.\n>\n> Set `enableRowRangeSelection: false` to preserve the previous non-range handler behavior. The handler must receive an event that exposes Shift directly or through `nativeEvent`; see [Shift Range Selection](./row-selection.md#shift-range-selection).\n\nThe \"some rows selected\" checks were simplified to mean \"at least one row is selected\":\n\n| API                                 | v8                                                  | v9                                            |\n| ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `table.getIsSomeRowsSelected()`     | `true` when some but not all rows are selected      | `true` when at least one row is selected      |\n| `table.getIsSomePageRowsSelected()` | `true` when some but not all page rows are selected | `true` when at least one page row is selected |\n\nIn v8 these returned `false` once every row was selected; in v9 they stay `true`. If you use them to drive an indeterminate \"select all\" checkbox, gate the indeterminate state on the matching all-selected check so it clears at full selection:\n\n`getIsSomeRowsSelected() && !getIsAllRowsSelected()`\n\n### Row and Internal API Changes\n\nSome row APIs have changed from private to public:\n\n| v8                                       | v9                                     |\n| ---------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `row._getAllCellsByColumnId()` (private) | `row.getAllCellsByColumnId()` (public) |\n\nAll other internal APIs prefixed with `_` have been removed. If you were using any of these, use their public equivalents.\n\n- Removed: `table._getPinnedRows()`\n- Removed: `table._getFacetedRowModel()`\n- Removed: `table._getFacetedMinMaxValues()`\n- Removed: `table._getFacetedUniqueValues()`\n\n---\n\n## Column Helper Changes\n\nThe `createColumnHelper` function now requires a `TFeatures` type parameter in addition to `TData`:\n\n```ts\n// v8\nimport { createColumnHelper } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst columnHelperV8 = createColumnHelper<Person>()\n\n// v9\nimport {\n  createColumnHelper,\n  tableFeatures,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ rowSortingFeature })\nconst columnHelperV9 = createColumnHelper<typeof features, Person>()\n```\n\n### New `columns()` Helper Method\n\nv9 adds a `columns()` helper for better type inference when wrapping column arrays.\n\n```ts\nconst columnHelper = createColumnHelper<typeof features, Person>()\n\n// Wrap your columns array for better type inference\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    header: 'First Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('lastName', {\n    id: 'lastName',\n    header: () => 'Last Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.display({\n    id: 'actions',\n    header: 'Actions',\n    cell: () => 'Edit',\n  }),\n])\n```\n\n### Using with `createTableHook`\n\nWhen using `createTableHook`, you get a pre-bound `createAppColumnHelper` that only requires `TData`:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createTableHook,\n  tableFeatures,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  sortFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst { injectAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({ features })\n\n// TFeatures is already bound, only need TData!\nconst columnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n```\n\n---\n\n## Rendering Changes\n\n### `FlexRender`\n\nThe rendering primitives in the Angular adapter are `FlexRender` and the `*flexRender` directives.\n\nIn v9, you can continue to render header/cell/footer content using the Angular adapter rendering utilities, but there are a few important improvements and helper APIs to be aware of.\n\n#### Structural directive rendering\n\nAngular rendering is directive-based:\n\n- `FlexRender` / `*flexRender` renders arbitrary render content (primitives, `TemplateRef`, component types, or `flexRenderComponent(...)` wrappers)\n- The directive is responsible for mounting embedded views or components via `ViewContainerRef`\n\n#### Shorthand directives\n\nIf you're rendering standard table content, prefer the shorthand helpers:\n\n- `*flexRenderCell=\"cell; let value\"`\n- `*flexRenderHeader=\"header; let value\"`\n- `*flexRenderFooter=\"footer; let value\"`\n\nThese automatically select the correct column definition (`columnDef.cell` / `header` / `footer`) and the right props (`cell.getContext()` / `header.getContext()`), so you don't need to manually provide `props:`.\n\n#### DI-aware render functions + context injection\n\nColumn definition render functions (`header`, `cell`, `footer`) run inside an Angular injection context, so they can safely call `inject()` and use signals.\n\nWhen a component is rendered through the FlexRender directives, you can also access the full render props object via DI using `injectFlexRenderContext()`.\n\n#### Component rendering helper: `flexRenderComponent`\n\nIf you need to render an Angular component with explicit configuration (custom `inputs`, `outputs`, `injector`, and Angular v20+ creation-time `bindings`/`directives`), return a `flexRenderComponent(Component, options)` wrapper from your column definition.\n\nFor complete rendering details (including component rendering, `TemplateRef`, `flexRenderComponent`, and context helpers), see the [FlexRender Guide](./flex-render).\n\n---\n\n## The `tableOptions()` Utility\n\nThe `tableOptions()` helper provides type-safe composition of table options. It's useful for creating reusable partial configurations that can be spread into your table setup.\n\n### Basic Usage\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  injectTable,\n  tableOptions,\n  tableFeatures,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\nimport { isDevMode } from '@angular/core'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ rowSortingFeature })\n\n// Create a reusable options object with features pre-configured\nconst baseOptions = tableOptions({\n  features,\n  debugTable: isDevMode(),\n})\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    ...baseOptions,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n### Composing Partial Options\n\n`tableOptions()` lets you omit required fields (like `data`, `columns`, or `features`) when creating partial configurations:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  tableOptions,\n  tableFeatures,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  filterFns,\n  sortFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n  filterFns,\n})\n\n// Partial options without data or columns\nconst featureOptions = tableOptions({ features })\n```\n\n```ts\nimport { injectTable, tableOptions } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\n// Another partial (inherits features from spread)\nconst paginationDefaults = tableOptions({\n  initialState: {\n    pagination: { pageIndex: 0, pageSize: 25 },\n  },\n})\n\nclass TableCmp {\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    ...featureOptions,\n    ...paginationDefaults,\n    columns: this.columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n### Using with `createTableHook`\n\n`tableOptions()` pairs well with `createTableHook` for building composable table factories:\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createTableHook,\n  tableOptions,\n  tableFeatures,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  sortFns,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst sharedOptions = tableOptions({ features })\n\nconst { injectAppTable } = createTableHook(sharedOptions)\n```\n\n---\n\n## `createTableHook`: Composable Table Patterns\n\n**This is an advanced, optional feature.** You don't need to use `createTableHook`; `injectTable` is sufficient for most use cases.\n\nFor applications with multiple tables sharing the same configuration, `createTableHook` lets you define features, row models, and reusable components once.\n\nFor full setup and patterns, see the [Composable Tables Guide](./composable-tables.md).\n\n---\n\n## TypeScript Changes Summary\n\n### Type Generics\n\nMost types now require a `TFeatures` parameter:\n\n```txt\n// v8\ntype Column<TData>\ntype ColumnDef<TData>\ntype Table<TData>\ntype Row<TData>\ntype Cell<TData, TValue>\n\n// v9\ntype Column<TFeatures, TData, TValue>\ntype ColumnDef<TFeatures, TData, TValue>\ntype Table<TFeatures, TData>\ntype Row<TFeatures, TData>\ntype Cell<TFeatures, TData, TValue>\n```\n\n### Using `typeof features`\n\nThe easiest way to get the `TFeatures` type is with `typeof`:\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n})\n\ntype MyFeatures = typeof features\n\nconst columns: ColumnDef<typeof features, Person>[] = [...]\n```\n\n### Using `StockFeatures`\n\nIf using `stockFeatures`, use the `StockFeatures` type:\n\n```ts\nimport type { StockFeatures, ColumnDef } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst columns: ColumnDef<StockFeatures, Person>[] = [...]\n```\n\n### `TableMeta`/`ColumnMeta` Typing Changes\n\nNo more declaration merging required! (Although it still works if you want to keep using it)\n\nGlobal declaration merging to extend `TableMeta` or `ColumnMeta` works exactly like it did in v8. The only change you need to make is updating the generics shape: both interfaces now take `TFeatures` as the first type parameter.\n\nOptionally, v9 also adds a new way to declare meta types **per-table** without declaration merging. You can use type-only `tableMeta`/`columnMeta` slots on the `features` option, which only affect tables created with that `features` object:\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  columnMeta: metaHelper<{ customProperty: string }>(),\n})\n```\n\nSee the new [Table and Column Meta Guide](../../../guide/table-and-column-meta) for full details on both approaches.\n\n### `FilterFns`/`SortFns`/`AggregationFns`/`FilterMeta` Augmentation Replaced by Registry Slots\n\nIn v8, making a custom function usable as a string reference (like `filterFn: 'fuzzy'`) required `declare module` augmentation of the `FilterFns` interface, and typing filter meta required augmenting `FilterMeta`. In v9, registering the function in the matching registry slot does both jobs with no global augmentation:\n\n```ts\n// v8\ndeclare module '@tanstack/angular-table' {\n  interface FilterFns {\n    fuzzy: FilterFn<unknown>\n  }\n  interface FilterMeta {\n    itemRank: RankingInfo\n  }\n}\n\n// v9 - register in the slot; the key becomes a valid string value\ninterface FuzzyFilterMeta {\n  itemRank?: RankingInfo\n}\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  filterFns: { fuzzy: fuzzyFilter },\n  filterMeta: metaHelper<FuzzyFilterMeta>(),\n})\n\n// 'fuzzy' now typechecks in column defs for tables using these features\ncolumnHelper.accessor('name', { filterFn: 'fuzzy' })\n```\n\nThe same pattern applies to `sortFns` (for `sortFn` string values) and `aggregationFns` (for `aggregationFn` string values). See the [Fuzzy Filtering Guide](./fuzzy-filtering.md) for a complete example.\n\n### `RowData` Type Restriction\n\nThe `RowData` type is now more restrictive:\n\n```ts\n// v8 - very permissive\ntype RowData = unknown\n\n// v9 - must be a record or array\ntype RowData = Record<string, any> | Array<any>\n```\n\nThis change improves type safety. If you were passing unusual data types, ensure your data conforms to `Record<string, any>` or `Array<any>`.\n\n---\n\n## Migration Checklist\n\n- [ ] Update your table setup to v9 and define `features` using `tableFeatures()` (or use `stockFeatures`)\n- [ ] Migrate `get*RowModel()` options: move row model factories into `tableFeatures` as named slots\n- [ ] Move `filterFns`, `sortFns`, and `aggregationFns` into `tableFeatures` as named slots (no longer passed as factory arguments)\n- [ ] Replace destructured row/cell/column/header methods with calls on the instance (for example, `row.getValue('name')`)\n- [ ] Rename `sortingFn` → `sortFn` in column definitions\n- [ ] Update column pinning to `start`/`end` terminology (`columnPinning.start`, `column.pin('end')`, `getStart*`/`getEnd*` APIs)\n- [ ] Replace `enablePinning` with `enableColumnPinning`/`enableRowPinning` if used\n- [ ] Rename `columnSizingInfo` state → `columnResizing` (and related options)\n- [ ] Convert custom aggregation callables to `constructAggregationFn({ aggregate, merge? })` definitions\n- [ ] Update state access: `table.getState().slice` → `table.atoms.<slice>.get()` where possible; use `table.store.get()` for full-state/debug reads\n- [ ] Update TypeScript types to include `TFeatures` generic\n- [ ] Update `createColumnHelper<TData>()` → `createColumnHelper<TFeatures, TData>()`\n- [ ] If you use `TableMeta`/`ColumnMeta` declaration merging, add the `TFeatures` generic to your augmentations (optionally, switch to the per-table `tableMeta`/`columnMeta` feature slots)\n- [ ] Replace `declare module` augmentation of `FilterFns`/`SortFns`/`AggregationFns` with registry-slot registration, and `FilterMeta` augmentation with the `filterMeta` slot\n- [ ] (Optional) Use `tableOptions()` for composable configurations\n- [ ] (Optional) Use `createTableHook` for reusable table patterns\n\n---\n\n## Examples\n\nCheck out these examples to see v9 patterns in action:\n\n- [Basic (Inject Table)](../examples/basic-inject-table)\n- [Basic (App Table)](../examples/basic-app-table)\n- [Filters](../examples/filters)\n- [Column Ordering](../examples/column-ordering)\n- [Column Pinning](../examples/column-pinning)\n- [Column Visibility](../examples/column-visibility)\n- [Expanding](../examples/expanding)\n- [Grouping](../examples/grouping)\n- [Row Selection](../examples/row-selection)\n- [Composable Tables](../examples/composable-tables)\n"}
